# `util.inspect` is a function of the library, in a file that loads at the first call. Its body is copied into the loop of the program, and there it reads a constant of its own file.
# Link's word "filled at every read" holds for as long as the function that holds the read runs. In front of the PROGRAM's loop nobody has loaded the file: the read stays in the turn. f0 = the program.
# RUN: walk f0 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = GetModuleVariable
